WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.433 --> 00:00:03.135
 Well Colton, Kevin,
congratulations, guys.

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:04.704
The two of you are going forward
in the third and final round

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.672
of the young guns competition.

00:00:06.772 --> 00:00:09.876
Now bladesmiths, we want to send
you back to your home forges

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.345
for four days to build this.

00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:18.018
NARRATOR: The German long sword.

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:23.789
The German long sword
traces its roots

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:25.859
back to 14th century Europe.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.627
This two handed weapon
was powerful enough

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:30.096
to deliver deadly blows
and its double edged blade

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.798
inflict deep wounds and
slashes against any enemy

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:34.567
that came across its path.

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:37.971
The massive blade was so
powerful that skilled warriors

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:40.139
had to train extensively
in the art of long sword

00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:42.275
fencing to master its strength.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.444
While this weapon was no
longer used in combat,

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:48.147
long sword fencing is practiced
around the world today.

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:50.082
 Both of you should be
on your A-game and bring

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:52.986
back your very best work.

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.487
Because at the end of
the day, only one of you

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:56.188
is going to be leaving here
with his second "Forged

00:00:56.255 --> 00:01:00.759
in Fire champion" title
and a check for $10,000.

00:01:00.826 --> 00:01:02.161
Bladesmiths, good luck.

00:01:02.227 --> 00:01:03.563
We will see you in four days.

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.637
 My name is Kevin Burgess.

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:12.738 line:14%
I am 22.

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:14.206 line:14%
I'm from Nacogdoches, Texas.

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:16.475 line:8%
I am currently a
full-time college student

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:20.080
and a part-time bladesmith Last
time I was here it was a blast

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:23.149
but I was about as entertaining
as watching paint dry.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.451
I decided that if I was
going to come back on here,

00:01:25.551 --> 00:01:27.820
I was going to try and
show people that I do

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.790
have somewhat of a personality.

00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:32.558
Ah, that's a really long blade.

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:35.461
If I mess up on a measurement
then it's all over.

00:01:35.527 --> 00:01:38.397
So it's just kind of check it
constantly, see where I am,

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:40.166
see whether or not
I've hit parameters

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.834
and just keep on
going from there.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.402
It's about to go
into heat treat.

00:01:43.502 --> 00:01:45.305
Just straight up,
straight into the oil.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.278
I'm noticing that
towards the tip it just

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:55.281
barely kicks off to the side.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:57.617
At this point, that
blade is a spring

00:01:57.683 --> 00:01:59.852
and it just keeps on
going back to exactly

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:03.490
where it was and I can't seem
to get it to go back straight.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.892
I couldn't get it out and
I just got to live with it.

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:08.294
But it does hurt my
chances at winning.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.663
I'm going to add
little cubic zirconium

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.631
diamonds to the handle.

00:02:12.698 --> 00:02:14.067
Cool.

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:15.535
I'm pretty worried about
the warp will send me home

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:18.204
but I'm hoping that my attention
to detail on the handle

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.873 line:8%
might be able to
carry me to a win.

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:24.477
My name's is Colton Arias.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.546 line:8%
I'm 20 years old and
I'm from Nebraska.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:29.815
When I first won "Forged in
Fire," I was 18 years old.

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:31.484
I was barely legal.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:32.585
But now I'm back.

00:02:32.651 --> 00:02:35.254
I'm 20 years old and
about 20 pounds heavier.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.157
So I've grown physically
into a larger human

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.760
and I've also grown my
skills in bladesmithing.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.561
From experience, I know
the greatest challenge

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:45.164
with any long sword build,
especially if I'm doing it out

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:48.234
of Damascus, is going to
be keeping it straight

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.503
and making sure the
temper and the heat treat

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.272
are spot on so it
does not break.

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:54.973
Plenty of things can go wrong
when you're clenching a sword.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:55.808
It could crack.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:56.742
It could warp.

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:58.111
It could fracture.

00:02:58.178 --> 00:03:00.279
Let's hope none of that
happens because everything

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.714
is riding on this quench.

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:09.488
Awesome.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:10.756
Perfect.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.224
This thing is massive.

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:14.194
In a build like this, a
million things can go wrong.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:17.063
If you make one false step
or try to rush it too much

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.298
you could ruin the whole
thing in the last step

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.900
or in the first step.

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:22.868
I'm completely done
with the sword.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:23.736
Fit and finish.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.371
It's damn near perfect.

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:28.474
That's a legendary sword.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:30.677
 Young "Forged in
Fire" champions,

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:33.613
welcome to the kill test.

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:35.414
To find out what
kind of lethal damage

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.716
your German long swords will do,
I'm going to take your weapon

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:41.053
and deliver some lethal
blows on this pig carcass.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:41.854
Colton, you're first.

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:42.654
Ready for this?

00:03:42.721 --> 00:03:43.923
 Do it.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.994
[music playing]

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:07.513
 All right, Colton, let's talk
about your German long sword.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.484
Every slice was a
very deep slice.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:17.957
Overall, the balance, the feel
of your sword it will KEAL.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:18.958
Kevin.
Your turn.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:19.658
You ready?

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.593
 You know it.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:27.800
[music playing]

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.679
 All right, Kevin,
those are very deep cuts,

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:42.515
almost cut through the
pig on the first strike.

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:45.951
Now earlier, prior to this, you
had a little bend at the tip

00:04:46.018 --> 00:04:47.586
but it didn't get any worse.

00:04:47.686 --> 00:04:51.724
Overall, your weapon,
sir, it will KEAL.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.792
 Thank you very much.

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:56.095
Doug almost went through
my pig on the first slice.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:57.663
I was really kind of
[clicks tongue] yeah.

00:04:57.729 --> 00:04:59.631
But it was not quite
enough to distract him

00:04:59.731 --> 00:05:02.201
from the warp in the sword so
he did end up noticing that

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:05.571
and that could be
what sends me home.

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:10.409
 Bladesmiths, welcome to the
strength test, the throne chop.

00:05:10.475 --> 00:05:12.111
In order to test the
strength of your edge

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:13.412
as well as the
overall construction

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.081
of your German long
swords, I'll be

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:16.648
bashing them into this throne.

00:05:16.748 --> 00:05:18.116
Colton, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:18.984
 Let's do it.

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:19.885
 All right.

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:25.525
[music playing]

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:47.647
 All right, Colton this is
a great looking blade, man.

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:50.049
I like your Damascus pattern.

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:52.484
It's still nice and
straight, didn't

00:05:52.551 --> 00:05:55.854
take much damage beyond a
slight glinting so well done.

00:05:55.954 --> 00:05:56.989
 Thank you.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.023
All right, Kevin,
you're up, man.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:05:59.058
You ready?
- You know it.

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:00.626
 All right.

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:05.732
[music playing]

00:06:28.954 --> 00:06:32.125
 All right, Kevin, well your
sword, it's all in one piece.

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.860
Again, the slightest of glinting
on the edge from contact

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:38.664
with the wood, but nothing
I would call damage.

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:40.800
You had a slight
warp to it coming in.

00:06:40.867 --> 00:06:41.701
That hasn't changed.

00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:42.601
It's the same.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:43.970
All in all, you
know, I think you

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:45.471
did a good job on your grinds.

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:47.906
The weight is good and it held
up great in strength test.

00:06:47.973 --> 00:06:48.841
Nice job.

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:49.609
 Thank you very much.

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:55.480
 All right, young guns,
this is a sharpness

00:06:55.547 --> 00:06:59.885
test, the cowhide bag slice.

00:06:59.985 --> 00:07:00.820
Colton, you're up first.

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:01.353
You ready for this?

00:07:01.454 --> 00:07:02.121
 Let's do it.

00:07:02.188 --> 00:07:03.255
 Let's do this.

00:07:03.322 --> 00:07:07.894
[music playing]

00:07:27.879 --> 00:07:32.218
 All right, Colton,
your edge cuts cleanly.

00:07:32.284 --> 00:07:33.585
It's razor sharp.

00:07:33.652 --> 00:07:36.522
In thrusting, drawing
it back, and cutting,

00:07:36.589 --> 00:07:38.457
the balance is good.

00:07:38.557 --> 00:07:41.894
And overall, sir, it will cut.

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:43.328
 Thank you.

00:07:43.395 --> 00:07:44.262
 Kevin, your turn.
You ready?

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:45.231
 You know it.

00:07:45.298 --> 00:07:46.232
 Let's do this.

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:50.470
[music playing]

00:08:04.616 --> 00:08:07.954
 All right, Kevin,
your edge, razor sharp.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.489
It cut cleanly all
through the bags.

00:08:10.589 --> 00:08:14.025
And overall, your
weapon, it will cut.

00:08:14.092 --> 00:08:16.662
 Thank you.

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:18.197
 Bladesmiths, throughout
this competition,

00:08:18.264 --> 00:08:20.032
you both have amazed
us tremendously.

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:22.768
But as you know, only one of
you can go home with the win.

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:26.439
The judges have talked it over
and they made a final decision.

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:28.007
The bladesmith going
home with a check

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:30.876
for $10,000 and his second
"Forged in Fire" champion title

00:08:30.976 --> 00:08:31.777
is--

00:08:34.747 --> 00:08:35.281
Colton.

00:08:35.348 --> 00:08:36.882
Congratulations.

00:08:36.948 --> 00:08:39.285
Kevin, you fought hard and you
brought us a beautiful blade

00:08:39.351 --> 00:08:41.587
but unfortunately, your time
in this competition has ended.

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:42.989
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:08:43.089 --> 00:08:45.424
step off the forge floor.

00:08:45.491 --> 00:08:47.026
 Peace.

00:08:47.092 --> 00:08:50.196
It turns out that I am not going
to be the two-time youngest

00:08:50.262 --> 00:08:53.366
champion but losing to
Colton, he's an amazing smith,

00:08:53.432 --> 00:08:55.500
does amazing work and
I'm glad it was him

00:08:55.567 --> 00:08:56.602
and not somebody else.

00:08:59.271 --> 00:09:02.141
 Well, Colton, that means
you are the youngest two-time

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:04.043
"Forged in Fire" champion
and you got yourself

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:05.978
another check for $10,000.

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:07.146
Congratulations.

00:09:07.246 --> 00:09:08.981
 Being the youngest
two-time "Forged in Fire"

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:10.916
champion feels amazing.

00:09:11.016 --> 00:09:13.319
I mean, this is probably one
of the closest competitions

00:09:13.385 --> 00:09:18.290
that I have seen and to come
out on top, it just feels great.

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:19.959
 Really, really well done.

00:09:20.025 --> 00:09:23.062
 My name is Colton Arias
and I'm the youngest two-time

00:09:23.129 --> 00:09:25.331
"Forged in Fire" champion.

